<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>By writing <m>{2.01}</m> as <m>{2} + ({0.01})</m>, use the first four terms of the expansion of <m>({2} + x)^{4}</m> to estimate <m>{2.01}^{4}</m>. Give your answer correct to 4 decimal places.</p><div><fillin characters="12" name="ans1"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Each term of <m>({2} + x)^{4}</m> is a row number times a power of <m>{2}</m> times a power of <m>x</m>: the powers of <m>{2}</m> go down while the powers of <m>x</m> go up. Put <m>x = {0.01}</m>.</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>r</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Row number</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{2}^{{4}-r}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>x^r</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Term</cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{1}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{16}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{1}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{16}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{1}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{4}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{8}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0.01}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0.32}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{2}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{6}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{4}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0.0001}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0.0024}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{3}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{4}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{2}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0.000001}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0.000008}</m></cell></row></tabular><p>The sum of the four terms is <m>{16.322408}</m>, so <m>{2.01}^{4} \approx {16.3224}</m> to 4 decimal places. A calculator gives <m>{16.32240801}\ldots</m>, which also rounds to <m>{16.3224}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{2040301}{125000}</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>